Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Explanation: ", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.003334184391727*^9},ExpressionUUID->"8a016596-5d3e-4d83-83d7-\
22293c6457fe"],

Cell["\<\
\[PartialD]f/\[PartialD]x(0,0)=0, \[PartialD]\.b2f/\[PartialD]x\.b2(0,0)\
\[NotEqual]0 means that the sections of the plane for any \[Micro] are \
locally parabolas (red), whose direction depends on the sign of  \[PartialD]\
\.b2f/\[PartialD]x\.b2:
\t- If  \[PartialD]\.b2f/\[PartialD]x\.b2>0, they are upward opening, meaning \
that the left arm for smaller x has a negative slope (stable) and the right \
arm for higher x has a positive slope (stable)
\t- The opposite is true for \[PartialD]\.b2f/\[PartialD]x\.b2<0
\[PartialD]f/\[PartialD]\[Mu](0,0)=0 means that at the bifurcation point, the \
blue slope is is constant (could be locally a parabola etc., but here it is \
simply a straight line); but \[PartialD]\.b2f/(\[PartialD]\[Mu]\[PartialD]x)\
\[NotEqual]0 means that the slope of the blue lines changes as x is varied:
\t- If \[PartialD]\.b2f/(\[PartialD]\[Mu]\[PartialD]x)>0, the slope goes from \
negative for small x to positive for high x\t
\t- The opposite is the case for \
\[PartialD]\.b2f/(\[PartialD]\[Mu]\[PartialD]x)<0
\t- In this case, \[PartialD]\.b2f/(\[PartialD]\[Mu]\[PartialD]x)>0 and \
\[PartialD]\.b2f/(\[PartialD]\[Mu]\[PartialD]x)<0 cause a mirroring of the \
plot along the x axis, meaning that the slopes of the red parabolas are \
inverted and as a result the stability behavior as well\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003333775644038*^9, 4.003333893524831*^9}, {
  4.003333926375339*^9, 4.00333407932025*^9}, {4.0033341691849937`*^9, 
  4.003334189129307*^9}, {4.003334539362136*^9, 
  4.003334609753689*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"30426305-ed4b-4284-86c9-\
6ba3beda537b"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

