071c2d9fa10d"],

Cell["\<\
- \[PartialD]\.b2f/\[PartialD]x\.b2 behaves the same way as for the \
transcritical bifurcation
- Here, \[PartialD]f/\[PartialD]\[Mu](0,0)\[NotEqual]0, meaning that the blue \
lines have a non-zero slope (in this case, they are even all parallel, \
meaning that there is no saddle)
\t- In this case, \[PartialD]f/\[PartialD]\[Mu]>0 and \
\[PartialD]f/\[PartialD]\[Mu]<0 cause a mirroring of the plot along the \
\[Micro] axis, meaning that the side where it crosses the x\[Micro] plane \
reverses (the parabola turns from left-opened to right-opened or vice versa)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003334302151854*^9, 4.00333432306955*^9}, {
  4.00333436626126*^9, 4.003334423266349*^9}, {4.003334621581787*^9, 
